  "prefLabel": "Saf-C 5605.23 Written Authorization",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Saf-C 5605.23 Written Authorization.\n\n(a) For the purposes of RSA 260:14, V(a)(10), a written authorization shall be submitted on letterhead.\n\n(b) The request shall contain the following:\n\n(1) Date of execution;\n\n(2) Name of life insurance company authorized to write life insurance policies in the state of New Hampshire, or its authorized agent;\n\n(3) The following information about the individual whose record is being sought:\n\na. Name;\n\nb. Address;\n\nc. Date of birth;\n\nd. Driver license number; and\n\ne. Signature of the individual whose record is being sought.\n\n(c) Approved written authorization shall be retained by the life insurance company, or its authorized agent, for a period not less than 5 years.\n\n(d) A life insurance company, or its authorized agent, shall produce approved written authorization upon request by the department, or its authorized agent.\n\nSource. #7621, EXEMPT, eff 1-1-02; ss by #13152, EXEMPT, eff 12-31-20",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/saf-c5600.html"
}
